== the repo-narrowed SKILL.md: what it holds and what it must not
### deployment section
$ sed -n /^## /,$p /tmp/grain-skill.wcaLRK/home/.claude/skills/grain/SKILL.md
    ## 1. Attribution & Session Setup
    
    Before running `grain` commands in an agent session, export your client identifier and session ID so tasks and comments record `filed_via` provenance (`X-Grain-Client`):
    
    ```sh
    export GRAIN_CLIENT="<tool>/<version>"
    export GRAIN_CLIENT_SESSION="<session-id>"
    ```
    
    Verify your active context, identity, scopes, and repository limits first:
    
    ```sh
    grain whoami --json
    ```
    
    Pass `--context narrow` (or `export GRAIN_CONTEXT=narrow`) when targeting this deployment explicitly.
    
    ## 2. Output Format (`--json`) and Exit Codes `0..5`
    
    Always pass `--json` when parsing results programmatically:
    - With `--json`, `stdout` contains a single valid JSON document using `/api` wire field names (`camelCase`). Human notes and staleness notices go exclusively to `stderr`.
    - When `--json` fails non-zero, `stderr` emits `{"error": {"code": "...", "message": "...", "fix": "..."}}` (except exit `1` on completed `wait` / `ci wait` / `ci show` queries, which emit the failed entity's JSON result on `stdout`).
    
    | Exit code | Meaning |
    |---:|---|
    | `0` | Success (for `wait` / `ci wait`, the wake condition was met cleanly). |
    | `1` | Target entity failed (e.g. CI concluded `failure`/`cancelled`, task closed unmerged/failed) or daemon `5xx`. |
    | `2` | CLI usage error, invalid flag/argument, state precondition conflict (`400`/`409`/`422`), or unknown context. |
    | `3` | Authentication or authorization failure (`401`/`403`, expired external token, login redirect, or bad file mode). |
    | `4` | Daemon unreachable (DNS/TLS error, connection refused, or HTTP connect/response timeout). |
    | `5` | Blocking `grain wait` or `grain ci wait` timed out (`--timeout` elapsed) before its wake condition was met. |
    
    ## 3. Core CLI Verbs
    
    - **Tasks & Inbox:**
      - `grain inbox [--repo <owner/name>] [--kind question|secret|notification|merge-held|proposal] --json`
      - `grain list [--repo <owner/name>] [--state <state>] [--filter filed_via:has:session=<id>] [--filter derived_from:eq:<owner/name#n>] --json`
      - `grain get <id> [--comments-since <RFC3339>] --json`
      - `grain create --repo <owner/name> --title "<title>" [--body "<md>" | --body-file <path|->] [--design <design/...>] [--depends-on <id>] [--field <k=v>] --json`
      - `grain reply <id> "<answer>" --json` (or `--body-file <path|->`)
      - `grain comment <id> "<note>" --json`
      - `grain logs <id> [--attempt <N>] [--tail <N>] [--follow] --json`
    - **Blocking Waits:**
      - `grain wait <id...> --until=awaiting-reply,ci-done,closed [--timeout=30m] --json`
      - `grain wait <id...> --until=merged [--timeout=30m] --json`
      - If `grain wait` exits `5` (timeout), inspect current task states in the output and re-run the printed `grain wait ...` command to continue waiting.
    - **Namespace (`ci://`, `task://`, `deploy://`, `config://`, `memory://`):**
      - `grain fs ls <uri> [--glob <pattern>] --json`
      - `grain fs read <uri> [--tail <bytes>] [--lines <N>]`
      - `grain fs grep <regex> <uri> [-i] [-C <N>] [--glob <pattern>] --json`
    - **CI, Pull Requests & Merge Queue:**
      - `grain ci list [--repo <owner/name>] [--branch <ref>] --json`
      - `grain ci show <run-id> --json`
      - `grain ci wait (<run-id> | --pr <owner/name#n> | --ref <branch> --repo <owner/name>) [--timeout 30m] --json`
      - `grain ci faults [--repo <owner/name>] --json` and `grain ci test-history <test-name> [--repo <owner/name>] --json` (check shared faults and flake history before blaming your change)
      - `grain ci retrigger <run-id> [--jobs <j1,j2>] --json`
      - `grain merge-queue [--repo <owner/name>] --json`
      - `grain pr adopt <owner/name#n> [--mode review-only|finish] [--spec <design/spec/...>] [--design <design/design/...>] --json`
      - `grain pr review <owner/name#n> [--design] [--spec <design/spec/...>] --json`
      - `grain pr status <owner/name#n> [--threads] --json`
    
    ## 4. Mandatory Safety Rules
    
    1. **Answer parked questions with `grain reply`, NEVER `grain comment`:** When a task is parked in `awaiting-reply` on an `ask_question` prompt, run `grain reply <id> "<answer>"` so Grain records the answer and re-queues the task. `grain comment` only appends a general note and leaves the task parked.
    2. **Never pass secrets through `grain reply` or `grain comment`:** When a task is parked on a secret request (`request_secret`), `grain reply` will refuse (`409` / exit `2`). Never ask the human to paste secret material into chat or CLI arguments; direct them to enter it in the encrypted input on the root-relative task page `[Task #<id>](/tasks/<id>)`.
    3. **Never call `grain force-merge`:** Force-merging bypasses merge predicates and is strictly a human operator override (`merge:force`). Inspect held gates with `grain merge-queue` and `grain pr status`, or re-enqueue a dropped change with `grain retry-merge <id>`.
    4. **Root-relative UI links:** Format all Grain UI references as root-relative paths such as `[Task #42](/tasks/42)` or `[Inbox](/inbox)`, never `http://localhost:...` URLs.
    
    ## 5. Active Deployment Metadata
    
    - **Context:** `narrow`
    - **Server:** `http://127.0.0.1:4301`
    - **Principal:** `agent:external:cli-debuerreotype-narrow-to7hh9`
    - **Scope set:** `grain/external-dev`
    - **Held scopes:** `ci:read@acme/allowed`, `ci:write@acme/allowed`, `deployment:read@acme/allowed`, `merge:write@acme/allowed`, `repos:read@acme/allowed`, `sandboxes:read@acme/allowed`, `tasks:read@acme/allowed`, `tasks:write@acme/allowed`, `templates:read@acme/allowed`
    - **`design/` workflow:** optional (pass `--design <design/...>` / `--spec <design/spec/...>` when targeting a repository with a `design/` directory)
    
    ### Reachable Repositories
    
    - `acme/allowed` (default target)
    
    ### Available Templates
    
    - `system:gke-sandbox-cluster` (Set up a GKE sandbox cluster)
    - `template-1` (allowed-fix) [repo: `acme/allowed`]
    - `template-4` (allowed-new) [repo: `acme/allowed`]
    - `template-6` (allowed-new) [repo: `acme/allowed`]
    - `template-8` (allowed-new) [repo: `acme/allowed`]
    
    ### Declared Custom Fields
    
    - None declared
    -> exit=0
